                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Only got this game because I had a coupon for it (or it was part of a bundle or something, honestly I don't remember). It's fun enough for what I got it for. \n\nGraphics are pretty simplified, so it could easily be mistaken for a port of a mobile game or kids game. There is a 'story' included, but I honestly kind of forgot about it halfway though playing so I could take it or leave it. Gameplay is your typical match 3 Bejewled-like, so not exactly reinventing the wheel or anything, but fun enough. It is kind of short, though. Like yeah there are over 100 levels, but for the most part it is easily beatable in one afternoon.\n\nPersonally I am an achievement hunter, so ordinarily not the type of game I would pick up (even if there weren't any particularly rare ones I'd still play it). Really only gave it a try because I was bored on a rainy day. Would say definitely hold off to get it unless it's on sale because it is not worth full price.",
